<title>FRANCE: Accor shares outperform bourse.</title>
<headline>Accor shares outperform bourse.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in hotel group Accor were up more than two percent at 1020 GMT, outperforming the bourse's blue chip CAC-40 index which was up 0.4 percent.</p>
<p>Brokers cited a report in the newspaper Les Echos that the town council of Dax was set to agree on January 8 on a definitive agreement putting Accor in charge of its thermal baths. Negotiations on a such a deal began 10 months ago.</p>
<p>Accor officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>One broker described the Dax activity as marginal for Accor. Its shares were up 13 francs, or 2.08 percent, at 637.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
